Report inotifyd's limit of 64 directories up front on Windows.
WaitForMultipleObjects() waits for at most MAXIMUM_WAIT_OBJECTS handles,
so with more directories every watch was set up and then the wait
failed at once with "watch failed: Invalid argument". Check the count
first and say what is wrong.

---
 miscutils/inotifyd.c |    4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

--- a/miscutils/inotifyd.c
+++ b/miscutils/inotifyd.c
@@ -333,6 +333,10 @@
 	argv++;
 	agent = *argv;
 	argc -= 2; // number of files we watch
+	// WaitForMultipleObjects() can't wait for any more
+	if (argc > MAXIMUM_WAIT_OBJECTS)
+		bb_error_msg_and_die("can't watch more than %d directories",
+								MAXIMUM_WAIT_OBJECTS);
 
 	watch = (struct watch *)xzalloc(argc * sizeof(struct watch));
 	hevent = (HANDLE *)xzalloc(argc * sizeof(HANDLE));
